resources.string:
Social Blocker+ uses the Android Accessibility Service API to:

• detect which app is currently on screen, so blocked apps can be closed and the daily time limit can be counted;
• read the address bar of supported browsers, only to recognise websites you put on your block list;
• read the text of Settings and installer screens, only to recognise screens that would turn this app off or uninstall it while you have blocking on ("Lock settings");
• show the eye-care break screen and the warm screen filter;
• tell the firewall which app you are using ("only while in use" rule).

This data is processed only on your device. It is never stored, collected, sent to a server or shared with anyone. You can turn the service off at any time in Android Settings when blocking is off.
